{
  "id": "Compound::DB00873 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Loteprednol, a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, is linked to Nr3c1 through a series of molecular interactions that involve steroid hormones. The evidence suggests that Loteprednol, as part of the broader class of corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists, binds to the glucocorticoid receptor (GCR) family, which includes Nr3c1. This binding is supported by multiple paths, all of which point to Nr3c1 as a target of corticosteroid agonists, with Desonide, Prednicarbate, and Desoximetasone all exhibiting a binding relationship with Nr3c1. The lowest common ancestors of these entities—Therapeutic Glucocorticoid and 11Beta-Hydroxy Steroid—highlight the shared role of corticosteroids in the biological response to stress and inflammation. The integration of these pathways underscores a consistent mechanism by which corticosteroids exert their effects, with Nr3c1 serving as a central hub in the signaling cascade. The evidence is robust and consistent, reinforcing the notion that Loteprednol's interaction with Nr3c1 is mediated through the corticosteroid receptor pathway.",
